Sorry if I was unclear; the PR doesn't break anything, but it does start to pull code into production bundles that has historically been able to be tree-shaken out.

This is the transitive closure of non tree-shakeable code:

```ts
function _throwError(dir: AbstractControlDirective, message: string): void {
  const messageEnd = _describeControlLocation(dir);
  throw new Error(`${message} ${messageEnd}`);
}

function _describeControlLocation(dir: AbstractControlDirective): string {
  const path = dir.path;
  if (path && path.length > 1) return `path: '${path.join(' -> ')}'`;
  if (path?.[0]) return `name: '${path}'`;
  return 'unspecified name attribute';
}
```

Possibly not too bad, but it does mean this change comes with a cost. There are many cases throughout the framework where we've opted to let production bundles crash instead of producing an error in support of smaller bundle sizes. Note that not DCE'ing error-related messaging is also being observed as a bug (e.g. #57034) which is counter to what #57236 is requesting.
